## Core Service Offerings

### High-Current Distribution
**Headline:** Heavy copper and busbar integration for extreme current demands.

**Intro:** Qmax Systems designs power circuits for environments where parasitic inductance and thermal bottlenecks can compromise the entire system. Engineers build heavy-copper stackups (4oz–14oz+), embed busbars, and optimize current return paths to eliminate hotspots.

**Applications:** EV inverters · Industrial motor drives · DC-DC converters · Welding equipment · UPS systems

### Creepage & Clearance
**Headline:** High-voltage isolation designed for safety certification from day one.

**Intro:** Qmax Systems designs high-voltage isolation to IEC 60601, UL 62368-1, and IPC-2221 for working voltages up to 1500VDC, building creepage and clearance into the board from the schematic.

**Applications:** Medical power supplies · EV battery management · Solar inverters · Industrial HV controllers

### Switching Noise Mitigation
**Headline:** Reducing conducted and radiated emissions in high-frequency switching designs.

**Intro:** Qmax Systems contains EMI at the source in high-frequency SiC and GaN designs, minimizing gate-loop and power-loop parasitic inductance, placing Pi-filters and snubbers optimally.

**Applications:** GaN/SiC converters · High-frequency DC-DC · Telecom rectifiers · Plasma generators

### Thermal Considerations
**Headline:** Thermal management engineered into the PCB — not bolted on after.

**Intro:** Qmax Systems uses insulated metal substrates (IMS), thermal via arrays, and specialized cooling interfaces to prevent junction-temperature violations.

**Applications:** LED drivers · Motor controllers · Battery chargers · Induction heating · High-power RF amplifiers

