## FAQ

**Q: How do you handle high-current requirements in small form factors?**
A: Heavy copper PCBs (up to 14oz+), busbar integration, and thermal via arrays, supporting 1000A+ DC sources.

**Q: What standards do you follow for high-voltage isolation?**
A: IPC-2221B for generic design and IEC 60601 (medical) or UL 62368-1 (IT/AV) for safety clearances and creepage distances up to 1500VDC.

**Q: How do you mitigate switching noise in SiC or GaN designs?**
A: Minimize loop inductance in gate-drive and power loops, place Pi-filters and snubbers, use 3D EM simulation to identify and suppress high-frequency harmonics.

**Q: Do you design custom magnetics for power converters?**
A: Yes. Core materials, winding geometries, and litz wire specified for custom inductors and transformers.

**Q: How do you validate thermal management?**
A: 3D thermal analysis to identify hotspots and optimize the interface between PCB, power components, and heatsinks.